```
.form-input:disabled, .form-select:disabled, .form-textarea:disabled { background: var(--clr-surface-subtle); color: var(--clr-text-faint); cursor: not-allowed; border-color: var(--clr-border); }
.form-input[readonly] { background: var(--clr-surface-subtle); color: var(--clr-text-secondary); }
```
- `.form-textarea` add `font-family` (inherits), plus `line-height: 1.6`.

Careful: `min-height: 44px` on textarea is fine.

Also add `input[type="file"]`? skip.

**Step 2: site.css** — add a new section near the map styles and a mobile block at the end.

I must be careful about CSS ordering: site.css has later overrides (many). If I add rules at the end, they win at equal specificity — good for responsive overrides.

New block at end of site.css:

```css
/* ============================================================
   Form controls & map pickers — responsive + accessibility pass
   ============================================================ */

/* Coordinates are LTR data — keep the pair from being reordered in RTL */
.register-coords-display,
.settings-coords-display,
