content.text:
Now the damage is quantified:

At 393px:
- hour select **37px wide**, font 13px, padding 6/8 → "09" + chevron clipped/overlapped
- period 53px
- remove button 20×32
- The whole row is 160px tall in 4 lines (day, 6 selects crowded, button)

At 1280 (desktop): hour 70px with 13px font and padding-left 8px — chevron at left 12px overlaps text. Also 13px is smaller than the rest of the UI (14px).

So the fixes:
1. Font 13px → 14px (`--fs-md`), and padding that respects the chevron (`padding-inline: 10px 30px`), no `!important`.
2. `.availability-row` desktop: widen hour/minute a bit (70 → 76) so "09" + chevron + padding fits at 14px. Actually with 30px left padding, 70px leaves 40 - 8 (right padding 10) = 30px for "09" (~22px at 14px) — fits. At 16px "09" ≈ 24px → fits 30. OK, keep 70.
3. Mobile (≤768): the flex two-line layout with 3 selects per line, sep full-width centered, remove on the day line at 44×44.

Let me now write the CSS. I'll replace the existing ≤768 block (7751-7780) and adjust the base rules (6853-6879 + 6921-6925 + admin duplicates 6927-6963).

Base changes:
- `.availability-row` desktop: keep flex, gap var(--space-2) → maybe var(--space-1) to fit more. At 768 with 16px font: day 110 + 70+70+95 + sep 13 + 70+70+95 + gaps 8*10=80 + padding 20 = 693. In the 1280 row width 1206 fine. Between 769 and 991: row width ~ 700 (container) → 693 fits barely. At 769 the .detail-card width ≈ 769-32-... maybe 705 content. Tight. Since ≤768 uses the new layout, at 769-991 it's the desktop flex row; needs ~693px. At 769 viewport, sidebar might be collapsed... risky.

Safer: apply the new mobile layout up to ≤991 (covers tablets where the sidebar is off-canvas). Then desktop (≥992) uses the flex row and has ~900px+ content. Hmm, at 992-1100 the content width with sidebar 260 = ~700 → still tight at 693. But it was already like that before (same widths, only font 16px vs 13px, and padding change might make it wider: 13px→16px doesn't change fixed widths; padding-left 8→30 adds 22px to each select? No — width is fixed (70px) including padding (border-box), so the text area shrinks but total stays 70. So total width unchanged ~640 at desktop.

Wait, at ≥992 my 16px guard doesn't apply (it's ≤991), so desktop font stays 14px (new) — select width 70 with 30px chevron padding leaves 40-10=30 for "9"/"09" at 14px (~20px) fine; period 95 leaves 65 for "صباحاً" at 14px (~46) fine.

At 769-991 font is 16px (iOS guard). Period 95 - 30 - 10 = 55 for "صباحاً" at 16px (~53px) — borderline clipping. So for 769-991, either widen the period to 105 or use the stacked layout.

