```
`#adminAvailabilityContainer .availability-row > *` = (1,1,0) beats (0,2,0) rules for width. And `.availability-row > *` (0,1,0) loses to `#admin... .availability-from-hour` (1,1,0)... wait `#adminAvailabilityContainer .availability-from-hour` = id(1)+class(1) = (1,1,0) vs `.availability-row > *` (0,1,0) → loses. So include the id-scoped selector for the wildcard too. Then individual classes get their flex basis from the class rules — but `flex: 1 1 calc(...)` on `.availability-from-hour` (0,1,0) vs wildcard `#admin... > *` (1,1,0) setting `flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1` (longhands) — the shorthand `flex` sets longhands with lower specificity → wildcard wins for grow/shrink; basis comes from the class rule (wildcard doesn't set basis). Result: basis calc(33%) with grow 1 shrink 1 → fine.

