Safer: reduce day basis to calc(100% - 60px) → 6px slack. Let me use 60px total (44 + 10 gap + 6). Actually gap is part of the line: basis = W - 44 - 10 = W-54 exactly fills. With -56 there's 2px slack. With -60 → 6px slack. Use `calc(100% - 64px)`? Then line 1 = W-64+44+10 = W-10, leaving 10px free which day absorbs (grow) → day ends at W-54, same as exact. So slack doesn't hurt; the day grows. Use calc(100% - 64px) for safety: day grows to fill exactly, remove stays 44.

Wait, if there's free space, day grows → its width = W - 54. Right. Good, use 64px.

